==Trivia==
*Nasi-Go-Round is a portmanteau of "nasi goreng", Malay / Indonesian for fried rice, which is the national dish of Indonesia, and "merry-go-round", a common amusement ride.
*Except for [[Poison on Rice]], each of these stages' names references a different part of Southeast Asian culture:
**[[Angkor S.W.A.T.]] is a pun on [[wikipedia:Angkor Wat|Angkor Wat]], a temple complex in Cambodia.
**[[Tropical Garden]]'s Japanese name, Tropical Choco Banana Garden, refers to chocolate-covered bananas, a popular snack in Southeast Asia.
**[[Kuala Lum-Pool]] is a pun on [[wikipedia:Kuala Lumpur|Kuala Lumpur]], the capital of Malaysia.
**[[Khao Man Guys]] is a pun on ''[[wikipedia:Hainanese chicken rice#Thailand|khao man gai]]'', a Thai chicken street food dish.
**[[Fish-Legged Beauty]] refers to the famous [[Mr. Mer|merlion statues]] of Singapore, though its Japanese name can also be seen as a reference to the song "HOT LIMIT" by [[wikipedia:Takanori Nishikawa|T.M. Revolution]].

